> Why does your body grow healthy[ …] or unhealthy cells[?]
Home » Blog » Why does your body grow[ healthy …] or unhealthy cells?
Look outside and see how[ fast] your garden is turning green. Spring acceler[ates cellular] growth[.] When cells multiply and divide[,] they duplicate their present condition. When mutated cells divide, they recreate their chaos and continue to do so[.]
How can you create healthy cells in a habitat of pollution[?] A body full of toxic wastes[,] heavy metals[, and] acidic chemicals is providing a perfect habitat for destructive microbes. When they take over, microbes create mutations inside your cells[.] Viruses, fungus[, and] bad microbes love toxic waste. They not only survive on it, but they also[ thrive on] it[!]
Harmony and wellness need a pure, clean, healthy environment. Ex[cess] acidic wastes are the underlying cause of degenerative diseases[ such as] diabetes[,] arthritis[,] fibromyalgia[,] rheumatoid arthritis, neurological disorders[, and cancer,] in[ fact,] all other diseases[.]
Springtime is the perfect time of[ year] to create wellness[ – to] join[ in] nature’[s heightened] healing[ potential.] Spring has always[ been] the[ time of year to] cleanse[, like] pruning the garden to make[ way for] new[,] healthy growth[.]
